s. Puede deberse a demandas estacionales o a necesidades específicas. El límite legal no refleja intenciones ilícitas.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos de diciembre atienden necesidades distintas. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas diferentes. Analizar si los contratos se distribuyen uniformemente entre los adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 77 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 10.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 7.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.3 to 11.2. December accounts for 38% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 29% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 13. Contract [1], for 14,250 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar trends could result from seasonal demand or budget constraints. The high number of contracts with one awardee does not prove misconduct, as it may reflect repeated needs or market availability.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts' dates and awardees to see if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Review the specific services or goods described in contract [1] to ensure they align with the body's needs. Verify if the same awardee was used for multiple contracts to assess if it reflects a pattern of repeated procurement.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["46W2FGeUi2nLIx6q1oPaMg%3D%3D","U%2BFVlJk%2F%2FOIaF6cS8TCh%2FA%3D%3D","QU6g%2BPrttDcUqXM96WStVA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}